# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages
#
# Palette pages are addressed by a slug of four HEX codes:
#   /palette/4e1f6e3e3e7545a9a998e8de/
#
# Only the top of the feed is pre-rendered (see PRERENDER_PALETTES in
# src/lib/data.server.js). The rule below catches every other address and
# serves it the same HTML. The page draws itself from the slug in the address,
# so the result is indistinguishable from a pre-rendered page.
#
# Status 200, not 301/302: this is a rewrite, not a redirect. The address in
# the browser must stay as it was, otherwise the client code cannot find the
# slug.
#
# The rule only applies to paths with no matching file, so genuinely
# pre-rendered pages are served normally and are unaffected.

/palette/*  /palette/index.html  200
